* sg13cmos5l-bandgap -- operating-point attribution deck for the FAILED `psrr_dc` row
* (issue #93). Template: sim/grid-run.sh substitutes @@VDD@@ and @@WORK@@ and writes the deck
* to sim/build/closed-loop-psrr-op/deck.cir. The model `.lib` cards, the temperature and the
* supply value come from the `klt sim` request (request-grid.json).
*
* THE FIXTURE IS sim/closed-loop-psrr/deck.cir.tmpl's, UNCHANGED. Every card line below is
* byte-identical to that template's -- same `Vpsrr` perturbation handle at the same deck
* default of `dc 0`, same `.options rshunt/gmin`, same `.global sub!` + `Vsub sub! vss dc 0`
* substrate tie (issue #83, decision record 0014), same `.include` and the same
* `Xdut vdd vref vss sg13cmos5l_bandgap_top` instantiation of the staged DUT (decision
* record 0013). Only this comment header differs, and sim/grid-run.sh strips `*` lines before
* it writes the deck. Checkable, and worth checking, because the whole point of this bench is
* that it reads the operating point THE COMMITTED PSRR GRID SOLVED, not a similar one:
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' sim/closed-loop-psrr/deck.cir.tmpl) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' sim/closed-loop-psrr-op/deck.cir.tmpl)     # must be empty
*
* The bench is its REQUEST, not its deck: request-grid.json runs the PSRR bench's own two
* `Vpsrr` = -0.05 V / +0.05 V secant solves, then a third `op` with `Vpsrr` altered back to
* 0 V -- a DC short, so that third solve is the unperturbed bias the secant was taken about --
* and reads every MOS device's operating point out of it with hand-written `@n.<path>[...]`
* expressions. Why hand-written and not `klt sim --op-lint`: the lint cannot address this PDK's
* OSDI (PSP103) devices (2AMLogic/klayout-tools#5637). See README.md and request-grid.json.
*
* A separate deck template rather than a second request in sim/closed-loop-psrr/: bench.json,
* the deck template and the request are one unit to sim/grid-run.sh, which takes ONE bench
* directory name, and sim/closed-loop-psrr/'s own files are cited by name in manifests/ and in
* decision record 0011. This directory is cited by neither and grades nothing.
*
* NO SPICE TITLE LINE (issue #19): `klt sim` `.include`s this deck into a top deck of its own,
* so line 1 here is not in title position and a title line would be parsed as a netlist element.

.options rshunt=1e9 gmin=1e-9

Vvdd vddsrc 0 dc @@VDD@@
Vpsrr vdd vddsrc dc 0
Vvss vss 0 dc 0
.global sub!
Vsub sub! vss dc 0

.include "@@WORK@@/bandgap_top.spice"
Xdut vdd vref vss sg13cmos5l_bandgap_top
